#question(title: [Challenge - 2])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  We want to calculate the value of
  $
    sum_(n = 0)^oo ((- 1)^n)/((2 n + 1) thin 3^n)
  $

  #box(width: 1fr, line(length: 100%, stroke: .5pt))

  + Compute
    $display(sum_(n = 0)^oo (- 1)^n x^(2 n))$
  + Compute $display(d/(d x) [arctan x])$
  + Pretend you can take derivatives and
    antiderivatives of series the way you can
    take them of finite sums. Which series
    adds up to $display(arctan x)$?
  + Now calculate the value of the original
    series.
]
